- `packages/graph-execution/src/agents/fixer.ts` (lines 19–60 options, 105–207 prompts, 222–298 `runFixer`: `currentHead`, `dirtyPaths`, `commitLeftovers`, `hasNewCommit`, `resetHard`, `git log --format=%B before..commit`, all with `cwd = integrationWorktree`).
- `packages/graph-execution/src/agents/reviewer.ts` (lines 26–57 `CodeReviewerOptions`, 96–205 `codeReviewerPrompt`, 210–241 `ReviewAgentOptions`, 256–407 `runReviewAgent`: throwaway worktree `path.join(runDir, "worktrees", "review-<label>")` created by `addDetachedWorktree(repo, worktree, head)` at lines 370–374 and removed at line 404).
- `packages/graph-execution/src/agents/tester.ts` (lines 10–35 options, 50–180 `testerPrompt`, 183–192 `runLiveTester`).
- `packages/graph-execution/src/git/git.ts` (lines 45–125: `addWorktree`, `addDetachedWorktree`, `removeWorktreeIfPresent`, `hasNewCommit`, `dirtyPaths`, `commitLeftovers`, `resetHard`; 161 `resolveRef`; 368–385 `rangeChanges`, `rangeFileDiff`).
- `packages/graph-execution/src/validate/commands.ts` (lines 11, 73–95) — `CommandsResult`, `runCommands(commands, cwd, signal, { parallel })`.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/runner/run.ts` (lines 524–553) — the run's `runReviewPhase` call and how `providers` are built for reviewers with their own provider.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/suite/orchestrator.ts` — `guarded` (lines 421–432), `afterIntegration` (lines 462–515: how a single-repo suite maps the phase result: drop, open findings, `codeReviewSkipped`, apply), `resumeSuite` (lines 198–239), plus the multi-repo code the previous task added.
- Tests to copy from: `review/phase.test.ts` + `__fixtures__/review-phase.ts` (fake provider, scripts), `review/context.test.ts` (temp repo + `commitFile`), `suite/orchestrator-e2e.test.ts` (lines 1–30: in-process prompt recording via `vi.mock("../providers/index.js")`; `until`, `withScript`, `recordingSpawn` from `__fixtures__/suite.ts`), and any multi-repo suite test/fixture the previous task added (grep `project.json` / `loadProject` in `src/**/*.test.ts` and `src/__fixtures__/`).

## Patterns to follow

Fake provider facts that matter here (`providers/fake.ts`): every non-summarizer agent writes `<label>.txt` (or the attempt's `write` map, paths relative to its cwd) and then runs `git add -A && git commit --allow-empty` **in its cwd** unless `commit: false`. A reviewer's `report` is written to the path in its prompt. Keys are `<role>:<label>`, e.g. `reviewer:code-r0`, `tester:tester-r0`, `fixer:fix-r1`, `fixer:fix-r0-v1`.

How the run builds reviewer providers (`runner/run.ts:525-530`):
```ts
const reviewers = await readRunReviewers(ctx.runDir);
const providers: Record<string, Provider> = {};
for (const name of new Set(reviewers.flatMap((r) => (r.provider && r.provider !== ctx.provider.name ? [r.provider] : [])))) {
  providers[name] = wrap(await getProvider(name, ctx.repo));
}
```

How the single-repo suite maps the phase result (`suite/orchestrator.ts:469-505`): `result.human?.decision === "drop"` → status `done`, result left on the branch; `result.exitCode !== 0 && !result.human` → `failed`; `codeReviewSkipped(result.reports)` → not applied, result left on the branch.

Errors: `AbortRunError(message, { step, hint })` / `InterruptedError` from `state/errors.ts`; hint `"graph-execution suite --resume"`.

## Step-by-step tasks

### CREATE `packages/graph-execution/src/review/workspace.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT** exactly these exports:
```ts
import type { CommandsResult } from "../validate/commands.js";

/** The git side of the folder the fixer works in. Heads are a sha (one repo) or a joint head `api=<sha> web=<sha>`. */
export interface FixerVcs {
  head(): Promise<string>;
  /** Uncommitted paths, as `dirtyPaths` lists them; prefixed `<repo>/` for several repos. */
  dirty(): Promise<string[]>;
  /** Commits what was left uncommitted, except `preexisting` paths; true when it committed anything (in any repo). */
  commitLeftovers(message: string, preexisting: readonly string[]): Promise<boolean>;
  /** True when HEAD has a commit `since` does not have (in any repo). */
  hasNewCommit(since: string): Promise<boolean>;
  /** `resetHard` to `head` (every repo): drops commits and tracked/untracked changes made since. */
  resetTo(head: string): Promise<void>;
  /** `git log --format=%B from..to`, newest first; for several repos each changed repo's log under a `[<name>]` line. */
  messages(from: string, to: string): Promise<string>;
}

/** What the review phase works on: the integration worktree of a run or suite, or the joint worktrees of a multi-repo suite. */
export interface ReviewWorkspace extends FixerVcs {
  /** The fixer's cwd: the integration worktree, or `<suiteDir>/worktrees/joint`. */
  dir: string;
  /** How log lines and errors name the result: `graph/<rid>`, or `suite/<rid> in api, web`. */
  label: string;
  /** The base of the diff: the starting commit, or the joint head of every repo's starting commit. */
  base: string;
  /** `git diff <base>..HEAD`, limited to `files` when given (`""` for an empty list); paths as the reviewers see them. */
  diff(files?: readonly string[]): Promise<string>;
  /** `git diff --name-only <base>..HEAD`, in the same path form as `diff`. */
  changedFiles(): Promise<string[]>;
  /** The text of each repo-root file that exists, by file name. */
  repoFiles(names: readonly string[]): Promise<Record<string, string>>;
  /** The validation commands as the fixer's prompt names them; empty means no validation gate. */
  checks: readonly string[];
  /** Runs every validation command; the failure names the command (and the repo). */
  validate(signal: AbortSignal): Promise<CommandsResult>;
  /** A reviewer's throwaway checkout of `head` at `dir`, and its removal (also of a half-created one). */
  addCheckout(dir: string, head: string): Promise<void>;
  removeCheckout(dir: string): Promise<void>;
  /** The changed files a reviewer's `files` globs select. */
  matchFiles(files: readonly string[], globs: readonly string[]): string[];
  /** Extra text for every reviewer, tester and fixer prompt (where the repos are, the path prefixes). */
  note?: string;
  /** Set when the live tester cannot run without a test plan: its report becomes `<notPerformed>: <this>` without an agent. */
  noPlanReason?: string;
}

export const formatHeads = (heads: Readonly<Record<string, string>>): string; // "api=<sha> web=<sha>", insertion order
export function parseHeads(text: string): Record<string, string> | undefined;   // undefined for a plain sha or a malformed value
export const shortHead = (head: string): string;  // sha.slice(0, 12), or each sha of a joint head shortened: "api=1a2b… web=…"
export const prefixPath = (name: string, file: string): string; // `${name}/${file.replaceAll("\\", "/")}`
/** Splits `api/src/x.ts` into { name: "api", path: "src/x.ts" } when `api` is one of `names`. */
export function splitPrefixed(file: string, names: readonly string[]): { name: string; path: string } | undefined;
/** The FixerVcs of one git worktree: today's behaviour of `runFixer`. */
export function worktreeVcs(worktree: string): FixerVcs;
export interface SingleWorkspaceOptions {
  repo: string; worktree: string; branch: string; startingCommit: string;
  /** Where repo-root files (REVIEW.md, TESTING.md, a reviewer's repoFile) are read from. */
  repoRoot: string;
  validate: readonly string[]; validateParallel: boolean;
}
export function singleWorkspace(o: SingleWorkspaceOptions): ReviewWorkspace;
```
- `singleWorkspace` must reproduce today's code exactly: `dir = worktree`, `label = branch`, `base = startingCommit`, `head()` = `git rev-parse <branch>` in `repo` (what `revParse(opts.repo, opts.integrationBranch)` does at phase.ts:627), `dirty/commitLeftovers/hasNewCommit/resetTo` = the `git.ts` functions on `worktree`, `messages(from,to)` = `git log --format=%B from..to` in `worktree`, `diff`/`changedFiles` = the git calls of context.ts lines 64–77 (cwd `worktree`, range `${startingCommit}..HEAD`), `repoFiles` = `readOptional(path.join(repoRoot, name))` (move `readOptional` from context.ts here and export it, or import it; `repoRoot` is `opts.repoFilesDir ?? opts.repo`, the option the reviewers task added to `ReviewPhaseOptions` / `ReviewerContextOptions`, so the single-repo e2e phase keeps reading them from its integration worktree), `checks = validate`, `validate(signal)` = `runCommands(validate, worktree, signal, { parallel: validateParallel })`, `addCheckout(dir, head)` = `addDetachedWorktree(repo, dir, head)`, `removeCheckout(dir)` = `removeWorktreeIfPresent(repo, dir)`, `matchFiles` = `matchFiles` of reviewers.ts. No `note`, no `noPlanReason`.
- **GOTCHA**: `parseHeads` returns a record only when every whitespace-separated token is `<name>=<hex sha>` with `<name>` matching `[A-Za-z0-9_-]+`; a 40-char sha alone returns `undefined`.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck`

