### UPDATE `packages/graph-execution/src/suite/joint.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT** (keep `jointDirOf` / `jointRepoDir` as they are):
```ts
export interface JointRepo {
  name: string; path: string; startingCommit: string;
  /** Its joint worktree: jointRepoDir(suiteDir, name). */
  dir: string;
  validate: readonly string[]; validateParallel: boolean;
}
export interface JointValidation { repo: string; ok: boolean; commands: number; command?: string; exitCode?: number; at: string }
export interface JointWorkspaceOptions {
  suiteDir: string; branch: string /* suite/<rid> */; repos: JointRepo[];
  /** Whether the project has a test-plan.json; without one the tester is not run. */
  hasTestPlan: boolean;
  /** Called after every validation with one entry per repo, in project order. */
  onValidation?: (results: JointValidation[]) => Promise<void>;
}
export function jointWorkspace(o: JointWorkspaceOptions): ReviewWorkspace;
export interface JointRange { name: string; repo: string; from: string; to: string }
/** `rangeChanges` of each range with paths prefixed `<name>/`, sorted by path. */
export async function jointRangeChanges(ranges: readonly JointRange[]): Promise<ChangedFile[]>; // ChangedFile from runner/events.ts
/** Creates (or keeps, on a resume) every joint worktree on `branch` and the sentinel repo at jointDirOf(suiteDir). */
export async function addJointWorktrees(suiteDir: string, branch: string, repos: readonly { name: string; path: string }[]): Promise<void>;
export async function removeJointWorktrees(suiteDir: string, repos: readonly { name: string; path: string }[]): Promise<void>;
/** Writes <suiteDir>/joint/spec.md and <suiteDir>/joint/tasks/test-plan.json (a copy of the project's, removed when it has none). */
export async function buildJointInputs(suiteDir: string, project: { dir: string; contract: string }, repos: readonly { name: string }[]): Promise<{ specPath: string; tasksDir: string; hasTestPlan: boolean }>;
// JointContext and JointResult stay exactly as the previous task defined them (see "What already exists").
export async function jointPhase(ctx: JointContext): Promise<JointResult>;
```
- `jointWorkspace` semantics (all git calls with `cwd` = the repo's joint worktree `r.dir`; `prefixPath` for every path going out, `splitPrefixed` for every path coming in):
  - `dir = jointDirOf(suiteDir)`; `label = `${branch} in ${names.join(", ")}``; `base = formatHeads({ [name]: startingCommit })`; `head()` = `formatHeads` of `currentHead(r.dir)` per repo.
  - `diff(files)`: per repo `git diff --src-prefix=a/<name>/ --dst-prefix=b/<name>/ <startingCommit>..HEAD [-- <that repo's unprefixed files>]` (skip a repo when `files` is given and selects none of its files; `[]` → `""`), joined with `"\n"`, empty outputs left out. `changedFiles()` = `git diff --name-only <start>..HEAD` per repo, prefixed, project order.
  - `repoFiles(names)` (this builds on the reviewers task's `repoFilesDir` idea: the e2e reviewers read repo files from the integration worktree; here from each joint worktree): for each file name, read it from every repo's joint worktree (`readOptional(path.join(r.dir, file))`); when at least one has it, the value is the texts joined as `## <name>\n\n<text.trimEnd()>` separated by a blank line.
  - `checks` = `repos.flatMap((r) => r.validate.map((c) => `cd repos/${r.name} && ${c}`))` (forward slashes on purpose: it is prompt text and also valid in `sh` and `cmd`).
  - `validate(signal)`: for every repo in order, `runCommands(r.validate, r.dir, signal, { parallel: r.validateParallel })` (a repo without commands is `ok` with `commands: 0`); never stop at the first failing repo. Call `onValidation` with one `JointValidation` per repo (`command`/`exitCode` from its failure; `at = new Date().toISOString()`). Return `{ ok: true }`, or one failure: `command` = the failures as `<name>: <command>` joined with `", "`, `exitCode` of the first, `output` = each as `## <name>: $ <command> (exit code N)\n<output>` joined with a blank line.
  - `dirty()` = `dirtyPaths(r.dir)` prefixed; `commitLeftovers(msg, pre)` = per repo `commitLeftovers(r.dir, msg, <pre of this repo, unprefixed>)`, true when any; `hasNewCommit(since)` = any repo `hasNewCommit(r.dir, parsed[name])`; `resetTo(head)` = `resetHard(r.dir, parsed[name])` per repo (throw `Error("not a joint head: ...")` when `parseHeads` fails); `messages(from, to)` = for each repo whose sha differs, `[<name>]\n` + `git log --format=%B <from>..<to>` trimmed, joined by a blank line.
  - `addCheckout(dir, head)`: `mkdir(path.join(dir, "repos"), { recursive: true })`, `initSentinel(dir)`, then per repo `addDetachedWorktree(r.path, path.join(dir, "repos", r.name), sha)`. `removeCheckout(dir)`: per repo `removeWorktreeIfPresent(r.path, path.join(dir, "repos", r.name))`, then `rm(dir, { recursive: true, force: true, ...RM_RETRY })`.
  - `matchFiles(files, globs)` = files matching `globs` either as prefixed (`api/src/x.ts`) or without the repo prefix (`src/x.ts`), so a repo's reviewer globs still work.
  - `note` (exact text, `<rid branch>` and names filled in):
    ```
    This change spans several git repositories, checked out under `repos/<name>/` of the current directory: api, web. The current directory itself is not one of them.
    - Paths in the diff, the findings and the review comments start with the repo name: `api/src/x.ts` is the file `repos/api/src/x.ts`.
    - Each repo is its own git repository on branch suite/<rid>. To commit, commit inside each repo you changed (`cd repos/api && git add -A && git commit -m "..."`), never in the current directory.
    - Each repo has its own validation commands; run them from inside that repo.
    ```
  - `noPlanReason` = `"the project has no test-plan.json"` when `!hasTestPlan`.
- `initSentinel(dir)` (not exported): when `dir/.git` does not exist, `git init -q` in `dir` and set local `user.name graph-execution`, `user.email graph-execution@localhost`, `commit.gpgsign false`. Why: the joint folder and the reviewer checkouts live inside the project folder's own git repo (under its ignored `.graph-execution/`); an agent (and the fake provider, which always runs `git add -A && git commit --allow-empty` in its cwd) that commits in its cwd would otherwise commit into the project repo. The sentinel catches those commits; the real work is in `repos/<name>`.
- `addJointWorktrees`: `initSentinel(jointDirOf(suiteDir))`, then for each repo, when `jointRepoDir(...)/.git` exists keep it (resume), else `mkdir` the parent and `addWorktree(repo.path, jointRepoDir(suiteDir, name), branch)` (the branch exists: the previous task created `suite/<rid>` in every repo). `removeJointWorktrees`: `removeWorktreeIfPresent(repo.path, jointRepoDir(...))` per repo, then `rm(jointDirOf(suiteDir), recursive, force, RM_RETRY)`.
