## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `review/workspace.ts` exports exactly the names and types above; `singleWorkspace` is the default and every existing test in `review/`, `agents/`, `runner/`, `suite/` passes unchanged.
- [ ] `phase.ts` no longer reads `opts.repo`, `opts.integrationWorktree`, `opts.integrationBranch`, `opts.startingCommit` or `config.validate` except to build `singleWorkspace`.
- [ ] Joint worktrees exist at `<suiteDir>/worktrees/joint/repos/<name>/` on `suite/<rid>` during the phase and are removed after an `applied`/`done` end; kept after `failed`/`aborted`.
- [ ] The joint reviewers' diff lists `api/…` and `web/…` paths; their spec contains the contract and every repo's spec; repo files are joined under `## <name>`.
- [ ] Each repo's validation commands run in its joint worktree after every fix pass; a failure names `<repo>: <command>`; `suite.json` `joint.validation` has one entry per repo.
- [ ] The fixer runs in `<suiteDir>/worktrees/joint/`, gets the note, and its leftovers are committed per changed repo with the same message; a fixer that changed no repo fails with "the fixer made no commit" and is retried.
- [ ] Without a project `test-plan.json`, the tester report says `live test not performed: the project has no test-plan.json` and no tester agent runs.
- [ ] `e2eReview: false` in the project config runs only the validation.
- [ ] A dropped human review, or a code review not performed, returns `keep` (applies nothing, ends `done` with the reason logged); open findings return `ok: false` and end `failed`.
- [ ] `suite --resume` after a stop in the joint phase continues there, restarts no feature, and applies each repo once.
- [ ] `suite/joint.test.ts` and the multi-repo e2e tests above exist and pass on Linux, macOS and Windows.

